+<p>
+  In most cases, the combination of resource type, canonical URL, and version will be unique on a specific server.
+  However, there are cases (e.g., <a href="valueset.html">ValueSet</a> resources with expansions,
+  <a href="structuredefinition.html">StructureDefinition</a> resources with generated snapshots, unassembled and
+  assembled <a href="questionnaire.html">Questionnaire</a> resources, etc.) where the same canonical version could
+  exist in multiple forms on the same server simultaneously. In these cases, clients will need to determine which form
+  contains the content needed. All forms should be identical in terms of meaning and definition.
+</p>
 <p>
   HL7 is developing a <a href="[%ig crmi%]">Canonical Resource Management</a> implementation guide 
   to define best practices for asserting and exposing local usage expectations of canonical and metadata resources.
